# Wave 6, editor-annotations. Closes the gap the annotation-anchor pillar
# deliberately left open (see that spec's resolved_annotation header).
#
# During a drag the editor does not re-render the SVG. It dims the moving
# elements and the overlay draws live geometry from scene/preview. Edges are
# re-routed there; callouts were not, so dragging an annotation or its target
# left the callout frozen at its pre-drag position until pointer-up.
#
# This is a separate pure module rather than an addition to scene/preview so
# that preview.ts is not touched at all: it already hands the overlay the
# moved bounds, which is everything a callout needs.

file: "packages/editor/src/scene/callout_preview.ts"
doc: "Live callout geometry during a gesture, computed from previewed bounds rather than the laid-out diagram."

methods: [
  { name: "calloutPreviews"
    change_type: ADDED
    doc:
      "One PreviewEdge per anchored annotation whose callout is affected by\n"
      "the bounds in `moved`, using those bounds for any element that appears\n"
      "there and the scene's resting bounds for any that does not.\n"
      "\n"
      "Affected means EITHER end moved. Dragging the target of a callout has\n"
      "to re-route it just as dragging the annotation does, and only one of\n"
      "the two ends is in `moved` in each case.\n"
      "\n"
      "An annotation with no anchor, or one whose anchor matches no element,\n"
      "contributes nothing.\n"
      "\n"
      "EDGE-anchored annotations also contribute nothing, and this is a real\n"
      "gap rather than a case that cannot arise: calloutSections DOES handle\n"
      "an edge target, taking its bounds from the polyline. The scene index\n"
      "built by buildSceneGeometry holds nodes, groups and annotations only --\n"
      "edges live separately in geometry.edgePolylines -- so an ElementBounds\n"
      "for an edge does not exist to compare against. The visible consequence\n"
      "is that an edge-anchored callout disappears for the duration of a drag\n"
      "and reappears on release. Accepted for this pillar because anchoring to\n"
      "an edge is rare and the alternative is indexing edge bounds, which\n"
      "belongs with the scene rather than here.\n"
      "\n"
      "PreviewEdge.id is the ANNOTATION's id. The overlay keys callouts\n"
      "separately from edges, so an annotation and an edge sharing an id do\n"
      "not collide.\n"
      "\n"
      "Geometry must agree with what the committed render will paint, or the\n"
      "line will visibly jump on pointer-up. Use edge_router's\n"
      "resolveAttachPoint for both ends with the same argument order\n"
      "calloutSections uses: the annotation end takes no hint and the target's\n"
      "centre, the target end takes the anchor's anchorPosition and the\n"
      "annotation's centre."
    inputs: [
      { name: "geometry", type: { named: { symbol: "SceneGeometry" } } },
      { name: "moved",    type: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ named: { symbol: "ElementBounds" } }] } } }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ named: { symbol: "PreviewEdge" } }] } }
    uses: ["resolveAttachPoint", "boundsCentre", "elementKey"]
  }
]
